## Memory Bank

- Update `memory-bank/activeContext.md` and `memory-bank/progress.md` after significant planning or implementation; user may say **update memory bank**.

## Skills

- Use `@cursor-memory-bank` for memory bank workflow.
- Storefront UX: `@frontend-design`; implementation: `@frontend-developer` (override Next version with `lagari-fe/AGENTS.md`).

## Backend notifications

- **Admin order emails** (`lagari-be/src/templates/admin-notification-email.ts`, `services/admin-order-email.ts`) must include the **full order snapshot**: customer name/phone/email, full address, line items with qty and prices, subtotal/discount/total, status, tracking, cancel reason, notes. Load via `loadAdminOrderSnapshot(orderId)` — never send sparse order admin emails.
- Admin links use `env.domain` (`DOMAIN` in `.env`, e.g. `https://www.lagari.pk`).

## Implementation gate

- **No** `lagari-be` or commerce UI until user approves P1 plan and says **execute** for P2+.

## Admin search filters

- **Debounce** text search (~350ms): local draft → URL commit → API fetch. See `docs/architecture/admin-ux.md` § Admin list filters & search.
- **Product/review search:** match **slug or title** (partial, case-insensitive); use `search-text.ts` on BE, `productSearch` query param.
- **Do not** hit the API on every keystroke; **do not** merge debounced values from stale React state — use `useDebouncedCommit` + URL noop guard.
- **Errors:** `ErrorBoundary` on providers; route `error.tsx`; queries show inline retry — never let one failed fetch crash the app.

## Resilience

- **ErrorBoundary** wraps storefront + admin providers (`components/errors/ErrorBoundary.tsx`).
- Route **`error.tsx`** on storefront and admin console; **`global-error.tsx`** at app root.
- Debounced URL commits: `lib/hooks/use-debounced-commit.ts` (ref-stable callback, no infinite loops).
- Invalid HTML: never nest block elements (e.g. `<div>`) inside `<p>`; `StarRating` uses `<span>`.
